1
00:00:00,074 --> 00:00:05,384
One patient. Booked to paid. — No cuts between systems, because there aren’t any.

2
00:00:08,878 --> 00:00:16,578
Front desk books a virtual visit.

3
00:00:16,578 --> 00:00:31,278
The type sets the duration and marks it virtual.

4
00:00:31,278 --> 00:00:34,962
It is already waiting in Telehealth.

5
00:00:34,962 --> 00:00:41,085
Patient, provider and time come with it.

6
00:00:41,085 --> 00:00:50,585
A Meet room is created and attached to the visit.

7
00:00:50,585 --> 00:00:56,182
Same patient. The chart already knows her.

8
00:00:56,182 --> 00:01:03,741
Findings go in once, and chart themselves over time.

9
00:01:03,741 --> 00:01:09,131
The visit becomes a claim.

10
00:01:09,131 --> 00:01:20,749
Her insurance comes with her.

11
00:01:20,749 --> 00:01:29,311
Codes are searched, not remembered.

12
00:01:29,311 --> 00:01:42,127
Money posts against the claim it settles.

13
00:01:42,127 --> 00:01:45,944
Receivables are right. Nobody reconciled anything.

14
00:01:45,989 --> 00:01:51,569
One patient. One system. — Booked, seen, documented, claimed, paid.
